1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,181
You step outside,

2
00:00:01,281 --> 00:00:02,778
and the rain smells like a

3
00:00:02,778 --> 00:00:03,259
hospital.

4
00:00:03,539 --> 00:00:05,318
What if it rained pure alcohol?

5
00:00:06,018 --> 00:00:07,493
Your hand turns freezing.

6
00:00:07,773 --> 00:00:10,474
Alcohol evaporates much faster than water,

7
00:00:10,574 --> 00:00:11,926
and it pulls the heat right

8
00:00:11,926 --> 00:00:12,747
out of your skin.

9
00:00:13,447 --> 00:00:14,879
Neighbors run out laughing,

10
00:00:14,979 --> 00:00:16,028
holding up cups.

11
00:00:16,308 --> 00:00:17,147
Bad idea.

12
00:00:17,427 --> 00:00:18,837
This is pure ethanol,

13
00:00:18,937 --> 00:00:20,671
far stronger than any drink,

14
00:00:20,771 --> 00:00:22,427
and it can poison you fast.

15
00:00:23,127 --> 00:00:24,903
Then the trees begin to change.

16
00:00:25,183 --> 00:00:27,257
Alcohol strips the waxy coat off

17
00:00:27,257 --> 00:00:29,205
every leaf and drags the water

18
00:00:29,205 --> 00:00:29,457
out.

19
00:00:29,737 --> 00:00:31,036
The green turns brown.

20
00:00:31,736 --> 00:00:33,121
The river won't save you.

21
00:00:33,401 --> 00:00:34,988
Alcohol mixes right in,

22
00:00:35,088 --> 00:00:36,410
microbes feast on it,

23
00:00:36,510 --> 00:00:38,143
and they use up the oxygen.

24
00:00:38,423 --> 00:00:39,515
The fish suffocate.

25
00:00:40,215 --> 00:00:41,759
But the real danger is in

26
00:00:41,759 --> 00:00:42,234
the air.

27
00:00:42,514 --> 00:00:44,302
Above thirteen degrees Celsius,

28
00:00:44,402 --> 00:00:46,596
alcohol gives off enough vapor to

29
00:00:46,596 --> 00:00:47,306
catch fire.

30
00:00:47,586 --> 00:00:48,683
One car engine.

31
00:00:48,963 --> 00:00:49,840
One spark.

32
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:51,743
And you may not even see

33
00:00:51,743 --> 00:00:51,888
it.

34
00:00:52,168 --> 00:00:54,318
Burning alcohol gives a faint blue

35
00:00:54,318 --> 00:00:54,677
flame,

36
00:00:54,777 --> 00:00:56,545
almost invisible in daylight.

37
00:00:56,825 --> 00:00:58,360
You feel the heat before you

38
00:00:58,360 --> 00:00:59,048
see the fire.

39
00:00:59,748 --> 00:01:01,102
Here's the strange part.

40
00:01:01,382 --> 00:01:02,737
That fire makes water.

41
00:01:03,017 --> 00:01:04,196
The steam rises,

42
00:01:04,296 --> 00:01:04,921
cools,

43
00:01:05,021 --> 00:01:07,079
and could fall again as ordinary

44
00:01:07,079 --> 00:01:07,391
rain.

45
00:01:08,091 --> 00:01:09,658
So this rain wouldn't get the

46
00:01:09,658 --> 00:01:10,307
world drunk.

47
00:01:10,587 --> 00:01:12,011
It would set it on fire.

48
00:01:12,291 --> 00:01:13,584
What should it rain next?

49
00:01:13,864 --> 00:01:14,794
Comment below.

